The '''[[Toyota]] KR engine family''' is a [[Straight-three engine|straight-3]] [[piston engine]], designed by [[Daihatsu]], a subsidiary of Toyota. The 1KR series uses aluminium engine blocks and chain driven [[DOHC]] cylinder heads. It uses [[multi-point fuel injection]], and has [[Multi-valve#Four valves|4 valves per cylinder]]. Some versions have [[VVT-i]] variable valve timing. The engine typically weighs {{convert|69|kg|abbr=on|round=5}} with all ancillaries but no fluids.

{{TOC limit|2}}

==1KR-FE==
The '''1KR-FE''' is a {{convert|998|cc|L|1|abbr=on|disp=flip}} version built in [[Japan]] and [[Poland]]. Bore and stroke is {{convert|71x84|mm|2|abbr=on}}, with a [[compression ratio]] of 10.5:1. Output is {{convert|67|PS|kW+bhp|abbr=on|0}} at 6000&nbsp;rpm with {{convert|91|Nm|lbft|abbr=on|0}} of torque at 4800&nbsp;rpm - and a rev-limit of 6500&nbsp;rpm - or {{convert|71|PS|kW+bhp|abbr=on|0}} at 6000&nbsp;rpm with {{convert|94|Nm|lbft|0|abbr=on}} of torque at 3600&nbsp;rpm. When originally on sale it met [[European emission standards#Emission standards for passenger cars|European emission standard EU4]] requirements and had {{CO2}} levels of 109&nbsp;g/km, but current applications meet [[European emission standards#Emission standards for passenger cars|European emission standard EU5]] and can have {{CO2}} levels as low as 99&nbsp;g/km.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://leasing.com/green-cars/peugeot/108/ |title=PEUGEOT 108: green cars with CO2 emissions under 120g/km |work=TheGreenCarWebsite |accessdate=2014-02-12}}</ref> This engine has been given the 2007, 2008, 2009 and 2010<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.autoblog.com/photos/mercedes-benz-amg-v8#3112998 |title=International Engine of the Year Photo Gallery |first=Sam |last=Abuelsamid |work=Autoblog |date=2010-06-24 |accessdate=2014-02-12}}</ref> [[International Engine of the Year]] awards in the sub-1.0 liter category.

The engine was also adapted to meet [[European emission standards#Emission standards for passenger cars|European emission standard EU6]] and can have {{CO2}} levels as low as 88/89&nbsp;g/km in [[Toyota Aygo]] or [[Citroën C1]]/[[Peugeot 108]] since 2014 in [[New European Driving Cycle|NEDC]].

