==1KR-DE==
[[File:Toyota Wigo G - Engine.jpg|thumb|1KR-DE engine in a [[Toyota Wigo]]]]

The '''1KR-DE''' is the non-[[VVT-i]] variant of the 1KR engine made by Daihatsu. It produces less power and [[torque]] than the 1KR-FE. Output is {{convert|65|PS|kW+bhp|abbr=on|0}} at 6000&nbsp;rpm and {{convert|85|Nm|lbft|0|abbr=on}} of torque at 3600&nbsp;rpm. Bore and stroke is {{convert|71x84|mm|2|abbr=on}}, while the [[engine displacement]] is {{convert|998|cc|L|1|order=flip|abbr=on}}.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.toyota.astra.co.id/product/agya/ |title=Toyota Agya - Specifications |work=www.toyota.co.id |accessdate=2014-09-17}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://daihatsu.co.id/products/specification/ayla |title=Daihatsu Ayla - Specifications |work=www.daihatsu.co.id |accessdate=2014-09-17}}</ref>

The 1KR-DE was specially designed for the Indonesian [[Low Cost Green Car (Indonesia)|LCGC]] (Low Cost Green Car) market to reduce cost. The cylinder head cover is made from a lightweight plastic-resin material. The [[exhaust manifold]] is integrated to the cylinder head together with the [[catalytic converter]] and [[oxygen sensor]] to save even more weight as well as helping the engine to warm up quicker, reducing total exhaust emissions. There was an overall saving of {{convert|10|kg|lb||abbr=on}}. <ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.otosia.com/berita/7-keunggulan-mesin-agya-ayla.html |title=7 Agya Engineering Excellence - Ayla |trans-title=7 Keunggulan Mesin Agya - Ayla |language=Indonesian |work=Otosia.com |date=2012-09-24 |accessdate=2014-03-04}}</ref>

=== Applications ===
* [[Daihatsu Ayla]] (2013–2023)
* [[Toyota Agya|Toyota Agya/Wigo]] (2013–2017)
* [[Daihatsu Hi-Max]], based on [[Daihatsu Hijet#tenth|tenth generation Hijet Truck]] (2016–2019)<ref>{{cite web |url=http://daihatsu.co.id/product/hi-max |title=Astra Daihatsu Indonesia - Daihatsu Hi-Max specification |work=Astra Daihatsu Motor |accessdate=2016-11-11 |archive-date=2018-05-18 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180518061235/http://daihatsu.co.id/product/hi-max |url-status=dead }}</ref>

==1KR-DE2==
The '''1KR-DE2''' is the more powerful variant of the 1KR-DE engine which is redesigned by [[Perodua]]. It produces {{convert|66|PS|kW+bhp|abbr=on|0}} at 6000&nbsp;rpm and {{convert|90|Nm|lbft|0|abbr=on}} of torque at 3600&nbsp;rpm. Like the 1KR-DE, bore and stroke are at {{convert|71x84|mm|2|abbr=on}}, respectively and [[engine displacement]] remains at {{convert|998|cc|L|1|order=flip|abbr=on}}<ref>{{cite web |url=http://paultan.org/2014/09/15/perodua-axia-launched/ |title=Perodua Axia Launched |last=Tan |first=Paul |work=paultan.org |date=2014-09-15 |accessdate=2014-09-17}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.perodua.com.my/ourcars/axia-advance/specifications |title=Perodua Axia Specifications |work=perodua.com.my |date=2014-09-15 |accessdate=2014-09-17}}</ref> The 1KR-DE2 achieves [[European emission standards#Emission standards for passenger cars|Euro IV]] emission standard and it is very fuel efficient due to the ECO Mode, where the engine will exchange drop one cylinder for every two cycles{{Citation needed|reason=Could not find any reliable search results to substantiate this feature claim.|date=September 2021}}, effectively achieving the economy of a {{convert|600|cc|L|1|order=flip|abbr=on}} engine, surpasses the 1KR-DE. The compression ratio for this engine is 11:1.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://paultan.org/2014/09/15/perodua-axia-launched/perodua_axia_specs_-008/ |title=Perodua Axia Launched |last=Tan |first=Paul |work=paultan.org |date=2014-09-15 |accessdate=2014-09-17}}</ref>

=== Applications ===
* [[Perodua Axia]] (2014–2017)

==1KR-VE==
[[File:1KR-VE.jpg|thumb|1KR-VE engine in a [[Perodua Bezza]]]]

The '''1KR-VE''' is a more powerful variant made by Perodua specifically improved version from the 1KR-DE2 which is made for the newest edition in the Perodua family.<ref>{{cite news |last=Tan |first=Danny |date=2023-02-14 |title=2023 Perodua Axia D74A launched – 1.0L D-CVT; DNGA; larger body; G, X, SE, AV variants, fr RM38.6k |work=paultan.org |location=Malaysia |url=https://paultan.org/2023/02/14/2023-perodua-axia-d74a-launched-1-0l-d-cvt-dnga-larger-body-g-x-se-av-variants-fr-rm38-6k/ |access-date=2023-02-16}}</ref> New 1.0-litre VVT-i engine is lighter & compact for better [[Fuel consumption in automobiles|fuel consumption]], better performance, reduced vibration & noise level. It was specifically made for the 1.0-litre variant for Perodua's first solely in-house manufactured car which is the Perodua Bezza. It is a modified and refined version of the 1KR-DE2 engine from the Perodua Axia. The new 1KR-VE engine produces {{convert|68|PS|kW+bhp|abbr=on|0}} at 6,000&nbsp;rpm and {{convert|91|Nm|lbft|abbr=on|0}} at 4,400&nbsp;rpm, offering a mild {{convert|1|hp||abbr=on}} and {{convert|1|Nm|lbft||abbr=on}} increase over the Axia's 1KR-DE2 plant. Perodua claims ECE fuel consumption figures of {{convert|22.8|km/L||abbr=on}} for the manual variant and {{convert|21.3|km/L||abbr=on}} with the automatic, both exhibiting a {{convert|1.2|km/L||abbr=on}} improvement over the old 1KR-DE2. The new 1KR-VE engine now features variable-valve timing with intelligence (VVT-i) on the intake valves. Several minor changes and refinements were also introduced for increased [[fuel efficiency]] and more linear power delivery. Notable changes include a higher 11.5:1 compression ratio, a high-tumble intake port, a longer [[intake manifold]], micro fuel spray injection and low-friction valve lifters.

